> f(x: i8) = (x/3)*3 + x%3
> id(x: i8) = x
> equiv f id
f and id are equal on the domain of f (exhaustive)
> g(x: i8) = x/2
> s(x: i8) = x>>1
> equiv g s
g and s differ at 64 points, e.g. x=-127: -63 vs -64
> p(x: u8) = x%8
> q(x: u8) = x&7
> equiv p q
p and q are equal on the domain of p (exhaustive)
> r(x: i8) = (-x)/3
> t(x: i8) = -(x/3)
> equiv r t
r and t differ at 1 point, e.g. x=-128: -42 vs 42
